---
/**
 * Contact page — the accountability surface E-E-A-T asks for (audit A2).
 */
import ContentPage from '../layouts/ContentPage.astro';

const email = 'epubstudioteam@gmail.com';
---

<ContentPage
  title="Contact — Epub Studio"
  description="How to reach the people who build Epub Studio: bug reports, broken conversions, corrections, and everything else."
  path="/contact"
  h1="Contact"
  lede="Epub Studio is built by two people who read what you send."
>
  <h2>Email</h2>
  <p>
    <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a> — for broken conversions, wrong
    answers in a guide, accessibility problems, or anything else. Corrections
    get priority: if a post says something your own test contradicts, we want
    to know.
  </p>

  <h2>Reporting a conversion problem</h2>
  <p>
    Everything on this site runs in your browser, so we never see your files —
    which also means we can't reproduce a failure from logs, because there are
    none. The most useful report includes: the tool's URL, what you dropped in
    (format and rough size), what you expected, and what happened instead. If
    the file isn't private, attaching it helps enormously; if it is, the
    error message shown on the page is the next best thing.
  </p>

  <h2>Who you're writing to</h2>
  <p>
    The site is built and maintained by
    <a href="/authors/mofid-ansari">Mofid Ansari</a> and
    <a href="/authors/shahid-ansari">Shahid Ansari</a>. No support tiers, no
    ticket system — a small inbox, read by the people who wrote the code.
  </p>
</ContentPage>
